<p>Hungary’s prime minister-elect Péter Magyar said on April 15 that his incoming government will suspend state media news broadcasts and move quickly on a broader package of reforms after his Tisza party’s landslide election victory ended Viktor Orbán’s 16 years in power. He said he wants a faster handover, with the new parliament convened in early May and his cabinet sworn in by mid-May, framing the transition as a chance to restore media freedom, judicial independence, and other democratic checks that critics say eroded under Orbán’s rule. The political shift also gives Hungary a chance to repair ties with Brussels and push for the release of suspended European Union funds that were frozen over rule-of-law concerns.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/beF_5Eyt5arU-6A2DDCE2O9VnuVYjn2lFdcFt0G_OrxPAVeQifdRmeKC2ZTOlFbQDJpZNmG-FzHuJdWpwkWR-Mgp9A95VEwG7mI5z3PSOyhdWFnGrN8aGGIU4cop7b3OyP0CYvSOB5rNsEKfGXKKZY1IqiDKwAc0Wqnj69r1jXmVob4rJ6gOw6lbPRCc8QKbr3Z55xmb777ut-SBKE2Q8fG-diUkr3xAivyjBmjPEHQtFHpLsPFfZ3PQvw' alt='Peter Magyar, leader of the election-winning Tisza Party, speaks to the media in Budapest on April 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>EU timetable: European Commission officials are due in Budapest on Friday to begin talks with Tisza, just days after the election and weeks before the new government is expected to take office.</li><li>Fuel focus: Magyar said he plans talks with MOL leadership, saying fuel supplies are his top operational priority in the coming weeks.</li><li>Council absence: Outgoing caretaker Prime Minister Orbán will skip next week’s informal European Council meeting in Cyprus, where Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico is likely to represent Hungary under Council rules.</li><li>Presidential standoff: Le Monde reported that Magyar warned his government would introduce a law to remove President Tamás Sulyok if the Orbán ally does not resign.</li></ul><blockquote>Every Hungarian deserves a public service media that honestly and accurately reports the affairs of our nation - Péter Magyar</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Péter Magyar: Magyar said he wants a faster handover of power, with the new parliament convened in early May. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2ddd0xyl5o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>DW analysis: DW said expectations at home and abroad are high because Magyar has promised a broad &#x27;system change&#x27; touching Hungary’s most pressing institutional and political issues. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-what-s-next-for-peter-magyar-after-election-win/a-76785927'>DW</a>)</li><li>Viktor Orbán allies: Reports on Magyar’s confrontation with state media and the presidency suggest that figures aligned with Orbán remain in office during the caretaker period and are resisting parts of the transition. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/hungary-prime-minister-elect-peter-magyar-suspend-state-media-propaganda'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350170/incoming-hungarian-leader-magyar-vows-suspend-state-news-broadcasts'>Incoming Hungarian leader Magyar vows to suspend state news broadcasts</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-what-s-next-for-peter-magyar-after-election-win/a-76785927'>Hungary: What&#x27;s next for Peter Magyar after election win?</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/commission-heads-hungary-budapest-friday-eu-funds-negotiations/'>Commission delegation heads to Budapest to negotiate release of EU funds</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/hungary-prime-minister-elect-peter-magyar-suspend-state-media-propaganda'>Hungary’s prime minister-elect vows to suspend ‘propaganda machine’ state media</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2ddd0xyl5o'>Magyar calls for fast handover of power in talks with Hungary&#x27;s president</a> - bbc.com</li><li